      "message": "fix(turning): refuse a helical modelled thread by name\n\nA turned part with a helical modelled thread (a SolidCraft M16x1.5)\ncould not be threaded, and the refusal named other causes: the slice\ncalled the STEP helix \"open\", and the axis fit said \"every axis fits\nthis model equally\". Threading reads a modelled thread as a revolved\nV section and cannot read a helix yet.\n\nAdd a helical-surface detector (multiaxis::axis_helix): about each\ncandidate axis, inclined facets state the screw parameter\nh = (n x u).(o - p) / (n.u) of the linear line complex of their normal\nlines; a revolve states zero, a helical thread one common nonzero h.\nThreading now refuses such a model with its pitch and hand, in the\nkernel and in the app arm before the slice of the job region.\n\nFixes #3023\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
